  "reason": "Complete construction and prerequisite audit; see research/phase-2-next-20-batch-4.notes.md and coverage.json. Source D, Lemma 4.3.6 pp.227–228, finite dominated specialization; documented alternative-proof disposition, no raw fetch claim. RN applies to finite positive Q and P with the common exhaustion Omega. Its density L is real integrable; event positivity and the zero-integral criterion give L>=0 a.s., and testing Omega gives E_P L=1. The conditional-expectation process theorem yields the martingale, and positivity gives Z_n>=0. For A in F_n the defining identity gives integral_A Z_n dP=integral_A L dP=Q(A), proving the restricted density claim. At n=N, conditioning a known L gives Z_N=L; at trivial F_0 the constant 1 satisfies all event tests. One may extend the finite filtration and Z constantly after N merely to fit N_0 notation. No assertion about infinite-horizon absolute continuity or Girsanov is included. AC is inherited from the Radon–Nikodym construction of conditional expectation; if a sequence of versions is needed, AC selects measurable versions at the countably many times. Identities remain identities of almost-sure classes, without completing the filtration.",
